  "details": "- CVE-2026-54872: pad the ladder scalar to a fixed, value-independent width\n  before the cardinality additions so EC scalar multiplication on curves using\n  the generic Montgomery ladder no longer leaks the scalar's magnitude by timing\n- CVE-2026-75805: guard the issuer and serial-number comparisons in\n  OSSL_CMP_exec_RR_ses() so a revocation response containing a CertId does not\n  dereference NULL when the certificate to be revoked was given as a PKCS#10 CSR\n- CVE-2026-75806: reject TLS 1.2 and DTLS 1.2 AEAD records shorter than the\n  mandatory explicit IV and authentication tag before AEAD processing, so a\n  short record is reported as bad_record_mac (TLS) or silently dropped (DTLS)\n  instead of raising a fatal internal error",
